# Build context excludes.  The image is built from the REPOSITORY ROOT
# (`docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .`), and backend/Dockerfile does
# `COPY backend/ /app/` — which copies whatever is sitting in that directory on
# the build machine.  Docker does not read .gitignore, so without this file a
# developer's backend/.env (Mistral + OpenAI keys, the login password) is baked
# into an image layer and travels with every push of it.  Deleting the file in a
# later layer would NOT remove it: layers are additive and readable.
#
# Credentials reach the container through the environment instead — see the
# `environment:` block in docker-compose.yml and the "Signing in" section of
# README.md.
#
# SYNTAX NOTE — these are NOT .gitignore rules.  Docker matches each pattern
# against the WHOLE path relative to the context root using Go's filepath.Match,
# where `*` does not cross a `/`.  So `.venv/` matches only a venv at the root
# and would sail straight past backend/.venv; nested matches need `**/`.  Every
# rule below is therefore either an explicit path or `**/`-prefixed.

# ---- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------
**/.env
**/.env.*
# .env.example is the documented template and carries only placeholders.
!.env.example

# ---- Local state that must never become image content ------------------
# The SQLite database holds real declarations; storage/ holds the uploaded
# invoices and packing lists.  Both are per-deployment runtime state (the app
# recreates them on first boot), not build inputs.
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
backend/storage
backend/split_job_id.txt

# ---- Host-specific build junk ------------------------------------------
# .venv is a Windows/macOS virtualenv full of absolute paths and native wheels;
# the image installs its own from requirements.txt (backend/Dockerfile line 8).
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/node_modules

# ---- Git / tooling / scratch -------------------------------------------
.git
.git1
.gitignore
.claude
ALL7_split
